; sketches.udon — toy document + provisional path strings for the paths spike
; NOT law. Spelling follows adjudication-2026-07 provisional + scenario habits.
; Bare paths appear only inside quoted strings or comments so this file
; remains ordinary UDON under today's CORE.

|sketch-pack[paths-spike]
  :purpose explore addressing without pinning syntax
  :date 2026-07-21

  |note[principles]
    Paths want to look like linearized UDON. References today are one
    segment. Tools want depth. Embeddability is the hard constraint.

  ; --- toy document the paths below pretend to address ---------------

  |config[app]
    |database[primary]
      :host db.example.com
      :pool 20
    |database[analytics]
      :host analytics.example.com
    |cache[redis]
      :url redis://localhost

  |user[alice].admin
    :email alice@example.com
  |user[bob]
    :email bob@example.com

  |order[123]
    :customer @user[alice]
    :sku SKU-9

  |el :x 1 :x 2
    stacked attribute on purpose

  |api
    :headers
      |header[auth] :value Bearer token
      |header[content-type] :value application/json

  |.defaults
    :adapter pg

  |step[1]
    integer key, not position
  |step["1"]
    string key "1" — distinct from integer 1

  |intent[42]
    :status open
  |intent["0042"]
    :status legacy-string-key

  |process[valve]?
    :health amber
    :fed-by @process[finding-routing]
    :fed-by @process[decision-surfacing]
  |process[finding-routing]
    :health green
  |process[decision-surfacing]
    :health green

  |section.intro
    prose lives here and currently has no path segment

  ; --- path catalogue (strings only) --------------------------------

  |paths[structural]
    :note root-to-leaf navigation
    |example :path "|config[app]|database[primary]:host"
      expect scalar db.example.com under at()
    |example :path "|config[app]|*"
      direct children of config
    |example :path "|api:headers|header[auth]:value"
      into node-valued attribute then child element

  |paths[relational]
    :note workhorse shape from day-in-the-life scenarios
    |example :path "||database[primary]"
      type-scoped key lookup any depth
    |example :path "||user[alice].admin"
      key plus trait AND-filter
    |example :path "||promise.capability"
      trait filter without key (scenario shape)
    |example :path "||.defaults"
      anonymous-only if mirror-document reading wins
    |example :path "||*.defaults"
      any element with trait defaults

  |paths[identity-purity]
    :note P1 collision site — do not treat integers as positions
    |example :path "||step[1]"
      integer key 1
    |example :path '||step["1"]'
      string key
    |example :path "||intent[42]"
      distinct from intent with string key "0042"
    |example :path '||intent["0042"]'
    |counterexample :path "|user[0]"
      stale doc meant "first user"; under identity purity this is key 0

  |paths[wildcards]
    |example :path "||user[*]:email"
    |example :path "||[primary]"
      any element with key primary
    |example :path "|config[app]|*[*]"
      all named children with any key — spelling may be wrong; probe later

  |paths[references]
    :note in-doc vs tool follow
    |example :path "@user[alice]"
      definition lookup / single-segment ref (live CORE shape)
    |example :path "@user[alice]:email"
      if multi-segment refs allowed later
    |example :path "||order[123]:customer@"
      follow attr ref to definition
    |example :path "||order[123]:customer@:email"
      follow then attribute
    |example :path "||process[valve]:fed-by@"
      stacked ref attr — at() vs all() diverge
    |example :path "||process[valve]:fed-by@:health"
    |example :path "||*:fed-by@"
      every fed-by follow (scenario multi-agent shape)
    |awkward :path "||*:*@"
      wildcard attr segment compose follow — confirm if intended

  |paths[stacked-attrs]
    |example :path "||el:x"
      at() last-value vs all() every assignment — open reading
    |example :path "||process[valve]:fed-by"
      at expects last assignment in host-scalar view; all fans out

  |paths[edit-tool]
    :note ops from test/scenarios — tool law candidates, not core
    |example :path "||intent[42]:status" :op set
    |example :path "||process[valve]:'$key'" :op set
      rename identity via designated attr
    |example :path "||promise[ore-and-soil]:'$traits'" :op add-value
      stack a trait; sugar-aware serialize may want .trait form
    |gap :path "(none)" :want "address third prose paragraph under section.intro"
      P7 — positional API on parent children may be enough for v1

  |paths[embeddability]
    :note how paths might appear as values someday
    |example :path-as-string "||intent[42]:status"
      today's only safe embedding
    |example :path-as-dialect "<path:||intent[42]:status>"
      self-delimiting future; interior free
    |counterexample :path-as-bare ||intent[42]:status
      would parse as structure, not a path value — do not do this today

  |paths[multiple-keys]
    :note OPEN S3 — under-exercised; spelling is pure guess
    |hypothetical :surface "|phase[9][scribal]"
    |hypothetical :path "||phase[9][scribal]"
    |question uniqueness "(type, key) or (type, key-tuple)?"

  |paths[deliberate-absences]
    :note not bugs unless demand insists
    |absent parent-step ".."
    |absent predicate "[?(:in = x)]"
    |absent glob "|foo*"
    |absent positional-index-as-identity-syntax
    |absent suffix-flag-filter "|process[valve]?"
      document has ?; path may not see $? today

  |at-all-contract
    :at "exactly one match or error"
    :all "explicitly plural — empty set is a result, not an error?"
    :note empty-set policy for all() not settled; at() empty = PathNotFound candidate

  |error-vocabulary-draft
    :note from scenario corpus — names not ratified
    |code PathNotFound
    |code PathNotUnique
    |code ReferencePlural
    |code PreconditionFailed
    |code SchemaViolation
